.\" Man page for loofi-fedora-tweaks
.TH LOOFI\-FEDORA\-TWEAKS 1 "2026-09-13" "27.0.1" "Loofi Fedora Tweaks Manual"
.SH NAME
loofi\-fedora\-tweaks \- reviewed Fedora maintenance for desktop users
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loofi\-fedora\-tweaks
[\fB\-\-cli\fR [\fIcommand\fR ...]]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loofi\-fedora\-tweaks
is a small PyQt6 desktop application for desktop\-neutral Fedora maintenance.
It separates read\-only inspection from reviewed system changes and shows the
result of each change independently.
.PP
When launched without options, the graphical interface opens.  Its five
destinations are Home, Updates & Apps, System Health, Protection & Recovery,
and Changes.  The application has no background service, local web API, or
Flatpak application distribution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cli " [" \fIcommand\fR " ...]"
Run the scriptable command\-line interface.  Remaining arguments are passed
to the CLI parser.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH CLI COMMANDS
The following commands are available after \fB\-\-cli\fR:
.TP
.B info
Show local system and platform information.
.TP
.B check [\fB\-\-target\fR \fITARGET\fR]
Run and persist the explicit read\-only System Check.  The target is selected
from the supported Fedora readiness profiles.
.TP
.B updates \fBcheck\fR|\fBconflicts\fR|\fBhistory\fR
Inspect package update availability, dependency conflicts, or recorded update
history.  Flatpak and firmware are separate update sources in the GUI and are
reported as unavailable when their host tools are missing.
.TP
.B troubleshoot \fBprofiles\fR|\fBrun\fR|\fBshow\fR|\fBlatest\fR|\fBcompare\fR|\fBexport\fR
Run or inspect a bounded, read\-only troubleshooting session and export its
redacted evidence.
.TP
.B changes \fBlist\fR|\fBshow\fR|\fBapply\fR|\fBverify\fR
Review Action Center plans and runs, apply one reviewed plan or named action,
and verify the resulting host state.  \fBapply\fR accepts typed \fB\-\-param
KEY=VALUE\fR values and requires explicit \fB\-\-yes\fR confirmation.
.TP
.B activity \fBlist\fR|\fBshow\fR|\fBrelated\fR|\fBrecover\fR|\fBexport\fR
Inspect the Trusted Change Journal and create reviewed recovery plans without
an automatic rollback.
.TP
.B doctor
Check dependencies, platform detection, state integrity, and authorization
availability without changing the host.
.TP
.B support\-bundle
Export a redacted support bundle for troubleshooting.
.SH GLOBAL CLI FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output a machine\-readable JSON envelope where supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Set the bounded operation timeout (default: 300 seconds).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show the planned operation without executing it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/loofi\-fedora\-tweaks/
Application directory containing Python modules, assets, and resources.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/loofi\-fedora\-tweaks/
User state, logs, plans, runs, journal records, and support exports.
.SH SECURITY
Persistent host mutations are routed through the Action Center and the
desktop's standard \fBpkexec\fR(1) authorization agent.  The application ships
no project\-specific polkit action files, never invokes \fBsudo\fR, never accepts
an arbitrary shell command, and never starts an unattended maintenance job.
Unknown platform or deployment detection fails closed.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at \fIhttps://github.com/loofiboss-bit/loofi\-fedora\-tweaks/issues\fR.
